tip: | Look at the bush. | Foliage is not one blob. It is a few 3:2 ovals overlapping, each lit on its own upper left.
tip: 3 | Light each cluster. | Every oval gets its own step of light, with the deepest dark where they meet at the bottom. Forms read from their shadows.
tip: 4 | Break the edge, then add berries. | Pixels knocked out of the rim make it leafy rather than smooth, and a checker of two greens does the same inside. A few red pixels last.
tip: | Try it. | Dither with a checker over the right side and watch it turn from flat green into leaves. | dither
